---
import './home.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f3f5f2" />
    <meta name="description" content="Checkride is an open-source project for verifying Kubernetes recovery. Explore the local drill validator, verification levels, and what is planned next." />
    <title>Checkride | Prove your recovery</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="inner header-inner">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Checkride home"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>Checkride</a>
        <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
          <a href="/comparison/">Comparison</a>
          <a href="/docs/">Documentation</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="header-action" href="/start/">Run locally <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
        <div class="inner intro-inner">
          <div class="intro-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> OPEN SOURCE · PRE-ALPHA</p>
            <h1 id="intro-title">Checkride</h1>
            <p class="lede">A backup completed. Can your application actually recover?</p>
            <p class="summary">Checkride is being built to restore Kubernetes applications into an isolated environment, check the data that came back, and show the evidence. Today, you can design and validate a drill locally.</p>
            <div class="intro-actions">
              <a class="button primary" href="/start/">Run the local validator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
              <a class="button secondary" href="/levels/">See verification levels <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="intro-aside" aria-label="Current development status">
            <span class="aside-label">CURRENT RELEASE / 0.1</span>
            <strong>Validate the plan.<br />Don't mistake it for the drill.</strong>
            <span>The local Studio checks a specification. Restore execution and evidence reports are still in development.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="preview-section" aria-labelledby="preview-title">
        <div class="inner">
          <div class="section-topline">
            <div><span class="section-number">01 / THE WORKBENCH</span><h2 id="preview-title">Start with a drill you can inspect.</h2></div>
            <span class="section-note">ACTUAL LOCAL STUDIO · NOT A HOSTED DEMO</span>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-frame">
            <img src="/images/studio-preview.png" width="1440" height="900" loading="eager" alt="Checkride Studio showing a fictional namespace-loss drill, JSON editor, planned verification levels V0 through V4, and a validation control" />
          </div>
          <div class="preview-caption"><span>Studio / drill validation</span><span>Import JSON · inspect the plan · validate against the local API</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="steps" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
        <div class="inner">
          <div class="section-topline"><div><span class="section-number">02 / THE METHOD</span><h2 id="steps-title">From a green backup to real evidence.</h2></div></div>
          <div class="step-grid">
            <div class="step"><span>01</span><h3>Define the failure</h3><p>Choose a scenario, target workload, recovery objectives, and the level of verification you need.</p></div>
            <div class="step"><span>02</span><h3>Restore in isolation</h3><p>Planned: rebuild in a separate cluster rather than trusting a backup status or healthy source environment.</p></div>
            <div class="step"><span>03</span><h3>Check what survived</h3><p>Planned: measure recovery time and data loss, then test application invariants and acknowledged writes.</p></div>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/levels/">Understand V0–V4 verification <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="status-section" aria-labelledby="status-title">
        <div class="inner status-layout">
          <div><span class="section-number">03 / HONEST STATUS</span><h2 id="status-title">Useful today. Not production-ready yet.</h2><p>Checkride is a master's thesis project in active development. It does not yet run unattended restores or certify compliance. Keep your existing backup and recovery controls.</p></div>
          <div class="status-list">
            <div><span class="status-indicator available" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>Available now</strong><p>Drill specification validation (Studio, CLI, API), test-data RPO ledger, disposable lab definitions.</p></div></div>
            <div><span class="status-indicator upcoming" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>In development</strong><p>Automated isolated restores, V0–V4 evidence reports, timelines, and CI recovery gates.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="next-step" aria-labelledby="next-title"><div class="inner next-inner"><div><span class="section-number">START SMALL</span><h2 id="next-title">Try a local drill specification.</h2><p>No cluster credentials or hosted account required for validation.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="/start/">Open the walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer"><div class="inner footer-inner"><span>Checkride · Apache-2.0 · Pre-alpha</span><div><a href="/docs/">Docs</a><a href="/comparison/">Compare</a><a href="/start/">Run locally</a></div></div></footer>
  </body>
</html>